      "content": "thanks. one more thing—the city council being stubborn about these \"unauthorized presences\" on the boundary is a bit of a headache. they seem to view any kind of encroachment as an aggressive intrusion rather than just a technicality. do you think there's any precedent for arguing that these minor trespasses are practically invisible or negligible to the neighborhood, so they don't need to be treated as major hostile threats to the zoning integrity?",
