      "content": "You can appeal to the concept of \"de minimis\" impact or \"practical irrelevance\" in your argument before the council. Frame the encroachment as a minor technicality that has no demonstrable negative impact on adjacent properties, light, air, or neighborhood character. Reference case law where courts have acknowledged that minor, visual intrusions, particularly those related to very old structures, do not undermine the core intent of the zoning ordinance. This shifts the argument from strict code adherence to equitable, practical land use.",
